==============================================================================
cond(C*C) as a power of cond(K), derived from a0_3_bounded_feature_family
   exponent = log(cond(C*C)) / log(cond(K)),
   cond(C*C) = ratio_cf * cond(K)   [ratio_cf is what the source stores]
==============================================================================
      decay       cond(K)    ratio_cf       cond(C*C)   exponent
   j^-0.5           11.91       22.38         266.688     2.2545
   j^-1.0           140.5       146.1         20533.4     2.0079
   j^-1.5            1815       782.9     1.42123e+06     1.8879

   An exponent near 2 is the claim: the bounded-feature route composes
   the covariance twice, so it squares the ill-posedness.  Reported to
   three significant figures in the manuscript.

